{"id":2378,"date":"2023-01-16T14:36:50","date_gmt":"2023-01-16T21:36:50","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/?p=2378"},"modified":"2023-01-16T14:38:42","modified_gmt":"2023-01-16T21:38:42","slug":"boulder-qas-2023-recommended-browser-device-list","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/boulder-qas-2023-recommended-browser-device-list\/","title":{"rendered":"BOULDER QA\u2019S 2023 RECOMMENDED BROWSER \/ DEVICE LIST"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">BOULDER QA\u2019S 2023 RECOMMENDED BROWSER \/ DEVICE LIST<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Each year we send our partners recommendations for Browsers and Devices for the coming year based on Browser and Device statistics.&nbsp; If our partners do not have access to website or application usage analytics or defined browser\/device specifications, then they use this data when sizing new projects for development and QA.&nbsp; With 2023 just begun we wanted to publish our recommendations to not just our partners, but to our readers as well. <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>With technology constantly changing with new operating systems, faster hardware and better screen resolutions its a challenge for us as technologists and our business partners to keep up with the latest trends and new hardware on the scene. We regularly check statistics to make sure that we are reviewing sites and applications using the best information available.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>We also wanted to share what devices that we have physically in our QA Lab as well as how we address devices that we may not have physical devices for.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>What browsers and devices are we recommending for 2023 and how do we come up with the recommendations for the coming year? This post is broken down into 3 sections:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"#2022-Recommended-Browser-Device-List\">2023 Recommended Browser \/ Device List<\/a><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"#Usage-Statistics\">Usage Statistics<\/a>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"#Desktop-Browser-Market-Share\">Desktop Browser Market Share<\/a><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"#iOS-Version-Market-Share\">iOS Version Market Share<\/a><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"#Android-Version-Market-Share\">Android Version Market Share<\/a><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>&nbsp;<a href=\"#Boulder-QA-Test-Lab\">Boulder QA Test Lab<\/a><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"2022-Recommended-Browser-Device-List\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-content-secondary-color\">2023 Recommended Browser \/ Device List<\/mark><\/h1>\n\n\n\n<p>The following outlines BQA\u2019s recommended Browser \/ Device List for 2023 based on the statistics we have obtained from Global Stats statcounter (<a rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" aria-label=\"https:\/\/gs.statcounter.com (opens in a new tab)\" href=\"https:\/\/gs.statcounter.com\" target=\"_blank\">https:\/\/gs.statcounter.com<\/a>).<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-content-secondary-color\">Browsers<\/mark><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Chrome: latest version available<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Safari: latest version available<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Firefox: latest version available<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Edge on Windows 11:&nbsp;latest version available<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-content-secondary-color\">Android Devices<\/mark><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Samsung A13 5G \/ OS 12 (Upgrade to OS 13 approximately Q1)<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Google Pixel 6 \/ OS 12<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Samsung S10 \/ OS 11<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Google Pixel \/ OS 10<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-content-secondary-color\">iOS Devices<\/mark><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>iPhone 14 \/ iOS 16<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>iPhone 12 \/ IOS 15<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>iPhone 8 \/ iOS 14<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>iPhone Mini \/ iOS 15<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>iPad 10th Generation \/ iOS 16<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>iPad Pro 10.5 \/ iOS 15<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Usage-Statistics\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-content-secondary-color\">Usage Statistics<\/mark><\/h1>\n\n\n\n<p>Boulder QA has reviewed a number of sites that provide market share statistics across platforms and operating systems. We really like the flexibility of Global Stats statcounter (<a href=\"https:\/\/gs.statcounter.com\/\">https:\/\/gs.statcounter.com<\/a>). Global Stats calculate their statistics on the basis of more than 10 billion page views per month by people from all over the world onto their 2 million+ member sites. Global Stats allows the user to review the market share on a worldwide basis or narrow it down to a specific market region, for example the United States.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>With a majority of the Boulder QA partners and users located in the United States we are able to view this specific region and provide a recommendation to our clients on which browsers and devices will provide them with the best coverage for the website or application. When we have a client outside of the United States, we can quickly adjust our inputs to their region and make recommendations with statistics to support their specific audience.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The following are the statistics BQA used to support our recommendations for 2023.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Desktop-Browser-Market-Share\">Desktop Browser Market Share&nbsp;<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>United States for the Last 12 months (Dec 2021 \u2013 Dec 2022)<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Chrome<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Safari<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Edge<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Firefox<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>60.14%<\/td><td>16.06%<\/td><td>13.8%<\/td><td>6.58%<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"616\" src=\"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/2023-01-16_14-26-02-1024x616.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2380\" srcset=\"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/2023-01-16_14-26-02-1024x616.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/2023-01-16_14-26-02-300x181.jpg 300w, https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/2023-01-16_14-26-02-768x462.jpg 768w, https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/2023-01-16_14-26-02.jpg 1894w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Source: <a href=\"https:\/\/gs.statcounter.com\/browser-market-share\/desktop\/united-states-of-america\/#monthly-202112-202212\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">StatCounter Global Stats &#8211; Browser Market Share<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"iOS-Version-Market-Share\">iOS Version Market Share<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>United States for the Last 12 months (Dec 2021 \u2013 Dec 2022)<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>iOS 16.1<\/strong><\/td><td><strong> iOS 15.6<\/strong><\/td><td><strong> iOS 16.0<\/strong><\/td><td><strong> iOS 15.7<\/strong><\/td><td><strong> iOS 16.2<\/strong><\/td><td><strong> iOS 15.5<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>47.75%<\/td><td>16.62%<\/td><td>12.93%<\/td><td>4.6%<\/td><td>4.3<\/td><td>2.86%<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"658\" src=\"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/2023-01-16_14-29-26-1024x658.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2381\" srcset=\"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/2023-01-16_14-29-26-1024x658.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/2023-01-16_14-29-26-300x193.jpg 300w, https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/2023-01-16_14-29-26-768x494.jpg 768w, https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/2023-01-16_14-29-26.jpg 1892w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Source: <a href=\"https:\/\/gs.statcounter.com\/ios-version-market-share\/mobile-tablet\/united-states-of-america\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">StatCounter Global Stats &#8211; iOS Version Market Share<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Android-Version-Market-Share\">Android Version Market Share<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>United States for the Last 12 months (Dec 2020 \u2013 Dec 2022)<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>12.0<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>13.0<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>11.0<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>10<\/strong><\/td><td><strong><strong>9.0 Pie<\/strong><\/strong><\/td><td><strong>8.1 Oreo<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>35.24%<\/td><td>22.03%<\/td><td>13.46%<\/td><td>11.76%<\/td><td>9.28%<\/td><td>1.81%<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"653\" src=\"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/2023-01-16_14-32-33-1024x653.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2382\" srcset=\"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/2023-01-16_14-32-33-1024x653.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/2023-01-16_14-32-33-300x191.jpg 300w, https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/2023-01-16_14-32-33-768x490.jpg 768w, https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/2023-01-16_14-32-33.jpg 1900w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\"><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p>Source: <a href=\"https:\/\/gs.statcounter.com\/android-version-market-share\/mobile-tablet\/united-states-of-america\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">StatCounter Global Stats &#8211; Android Version Market Share<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Boulder-QA-Test-Lab\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-content-secondary-color\">Boulder QA Test Lab<\/mark><\/h1>\n\n\n\n<p>The following is a list of physical devices that BQA currently has in their lab.&nbsp; We also use BrowserStack (<a href=\"https:\/\/www.browserstack.com\/\">https:\/\/www.browserstack.com<\/a>) to supplement the physical devices that we have in inventory.&nbsp; BrowserStack provides BQA the ability to review websites on devices that we may not currently have in our Test Lab or if a client has a very specific device that they would like reviewed.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>While we believe the best review of any website or application is on a physical device, we have found that BrowserStack provides us the ability to expand our lab with confidence for specific client requests that may occur outside of physical devices that we currently have outside of our lab.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>We have also used BrowserStack to help identify issues which may always be repeatable within our client\u2019s development environment. There have been cases where we have reported an issue to our development partners that they cannot reproduce in house. Using BrowserStack to verify the issue and allowing us to share those results with our development partners increases the ability to provide a quality product to the end users.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Desktops<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>MacBook Pro<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Windows 11 (Physical and Virtual Machines)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">iOS Devices<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>iPhone 14 \/ iOS 16<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>iPhone 12 \/ iOS 15<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>iPhone 12 Mini \/ iOS 16<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>iPhone 8 \/ iOS 14<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>iPhone 7P \/ iOS 14<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>iPad (10th Generation) \/ iOS 16<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>iPad Pro 10.5 \/ iOS 16<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>iPad Mini 4 \/ iOS 15<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Android Devices<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Samsung A13 5G \/ OS 12 (Upgrade to OS 13 approximately Q1)<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Google Pixel 6 \/ OS 12<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Samsung S10 \/ OS 11<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Google Pixel \/ OS 10<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>BOULDER QA\u2019S 2023 RECOMMENDED BROWSER \/ DEVICE LIST Each year we send our partners recommendations for Browsers and Devices for the coming year based on Browser and Device statistics.&nbsp; If our partners do not have access to website or application usage analytics or defined browser\/device specifications, then they use this data when sizing new projects&#8230;<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":2338,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[1],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-2378","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-uncategorized"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/2378","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=2378"}],"version-history":[{"count":2,"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/2378\/revisions"}],"pred